Example: Restrict access to a specific Region
The following policy denies users permission to use all Amazon EC2 API actions unless the
      Region is Europe (Frankfurt). It uses the global condition key
aws:RequestedRegion
, which is supported by all Amazon EC2 API actions.
JSON
{
"Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "ec2:*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition":
{
"StringNotEquals":
{
"aws:RequestedRegion": "eu-central-1"
        }
      }
    }  
  ]
}
Alternatively, you can use the condition key
ec2:Region
, which is specific to
            Amazon EC2 and is supported by all Amazon EC2 API actions.
JSON
{
"Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "ec2:*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition":
{
"StringNotEquals":
{
"ec2:Region": "eu-central-1"
        }
      }
    }  
  ]
}
